 "note": [
  "Scripture came from the Indian Revised Version (IRV Hindi, irvhin) — the text `language_seed.py` records for this language — parsed whole from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx; 31,104 verses, section headings, notes and cross-reference apparatus stripped). Translators looked up every quotation, cited or not.",
  "A `mined` row means the translator reported the quotation as pasted verbatim AND the finished chapter body contains an exact substring of that IRV verse of at least 45 characters (or ≥90% of a shorter verse) — measured, not claimed. A verse re-personed, re-tensed or re-aimed to fit Bounds's sentence is self_rendered even where a long span matches. `block_index` is a GLOBAL 0-based index over the book's blocks in chapter order.",
  "Isaiah 45:11 (chs 3 and 9) is self_rendered on purpose: the IRV renders it as rhetorical questions, which reverses Bounds's reading of \"command ye Me\"; the IRV vocabulary was kept with the clauses recast as imperatives. Flagged for native review.",
  "Bounds quotes other preachers (Gilmour, Brainerd, Payson, Wesley…) at least as often as the Bible; those are reported speech, not recorded here."
